text:
emma_csm: Heads-up  Ember preview cohort slow to onboard  9/25 seats active, two accounts flagged for low engagement. Want to run a short 'sticky paths' program to drive value quickly.

priya_pm: Agree. Sticky paths = 5-10 minute guided wins inside the product + a 20m office hour. If we get 50% of seats to run a test, renewal signals should improve.

ryan_se: I can prepare a tiny sample app (Go + Node snippets) that demonstrates embeddings + reranking with a pre-seeded dataset. Keep it under 20 lines so customers can copy/paste.

carlos_enable: Ill build the in-product micro-tour and a 1-click 'Run Lab' button that links to the repo. Also propose a micro-incentive: feature badge + $100 usage credit for 3 active users.

opsbot: draft calendar event created: Ember preview  Sticky paths lab  Tue Apr 6, 10:00 PT / 18:00 CET. link: https://calendar.redwood.com/event/ember-sticky-3421

emma_csm: For measurement, we'll track: RSVP -> lab run (binary), WAU delta at 7d, and renewal intent in the post-session pulse. Priya  can you draft the 3-question pulse?

priya_pm: Draft pulse: 1) Did you run the lab? (y/n) 2) In the next 30d, likely to increase seats? (scale 1-5) 3) Biggest blocker to shipping (free text). I'll put it in the invite as a quick form.

ryan_se: Snippet preview (inline, will push full repo):
```
# node quick example
const R = require('redwood');
const c = new R.Client({apiKey: process.env.RD_KEY});
(async ()=>{
  const res = await c.embeddings.create({model:'tiny-embed', input:['doc A','doc B']});
  const rr = await c.rerank({model:'tiny-rank', query:'invoice 123', documents:['doc A','doc B']});
  console.log(rr);
})();
```

carlos_enable: I'll localize the micro-tour copy for EMEA and add a second session at 16:30 UK time. Also will draft two outreach email subjects to A/B: "Run a 10m lab: see rerank in action" vs "Quick win: improve search relevance for Ember".

emma_csm: Two at-risk orgs: Ember-Intl (ARR $22k) and Ember-Docs (ARR $9k). I'll propose the badge + credit for Ember-Intl and do targeted 1:1 outreach to Ember-Docs with a security-friendly demo.

priya_pm: Landing page checklist: 1) quick agenda, 2) repo link, 3) pulse form, 4) support contact. I'll publish by EOD tomorrow.

ryan_se: Will upload full repo + one-click run instructions to shared drive by EOD today. Will include a dockerized example for air-gapped trials.

carlos_enable: Action list: Ryan - repo + docker demo (EOD), Priya - pulse + landing (tomorrow AM), Carlos - micro-tour + EMEA session (Thu EOD), Emma - targeted outreach + reward approval with finance. Reconvene Mon 9am PT to review RSVPs.

emma_csm: Noted. If RSVP < 30% by Sun noon, we pivot to bespoke 1:1 sessions for the two at-risk accounts.

opsbot: thread will auto-archive after 7 days of inactivity.
